  "prefLabel": "He-P 1903.03 Complainant Confidentiality",
  "priorExpiration": "2018-11-20",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "He-P 1903.03 Complainant Confidentiality. Confidentiality of the complainant shall be protected pursuant to RSA 155:74, II, as follows:\n\n(a) In accordance with RSA 91-A, all information contained in a complaint shall be furnished to the public upon request, except the complainant’s name, which shall not be supplied without express written approval of the complainant;\n\n(b) All physical copies of complaints shall be stored in a receptacle secured from public or unrestricted access, such as a locked file cabinet, when not in use; and\n\n(c) Electronic information regarding complaints that include the complainant’s name shall be stored on a computer hard drive(s) or disk(s) and be secured from unauthorized access, as follows:\n\n(1) Removable disks which contain such data shall be secured in the same manner as physical copies, as detailed in He-P 1903.03(b); and\n\n(2) Non-removable disks or computer hard drives which contain such data shall be secured by using password protection of those computer files.\n\nSource. #9054, eff 12-29-07, EXPIRED: 12-29-15\n\nNew. #12534, INTERIM, eff 5-24-18, EXPIRES: 11-20-18; ss by #12677, eff 11-20-18",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-p1900.html"
}
